  modulo uses positive divisors 3 and 4; the implementation uses only constructs
  modeled by the supplied semantics. Non-integer inputs and their exceptions
  are outside the stated domain.
- **B3:** the fold is formally defined index-by-index with the same precedence
  and arithmetic as the requested result. It is not an opaque result oracle.
- **B4:** the implementation returns the requested transformed sum, preserves
  the input list, and passes all three prompt examples under both CPython and
